'''Sanu-Sasso Prima FC''', commonly referred to as '''Prima''' or '''I Njaxas''' (Waajuri: ''The Panthers''), is a professional [[association football|football]] club based in [[District 2, Sanu-Sasso|District 2]] of [[Sanu-Sasso]], [[Asikyira]]. The club competes in the [[Asikyiran Premier League]], the top tier of Asikyiran football, and is widely regarded as one of the most successful and prestigious football clubs in [[Adonia]].

Founded in 1906, Prima is one of the oldest football clubs in Asikyira and has won the Asikyiran Premier League a record 14 times. The club has also won the [[Asikyiran Cup]] 9 times and the [[Abyalan Champions' Cup]] twice (2012, 2021), making it the most successful Asikyiran club in continental competition. Prima's home ground is the [[Stadiu di Distrettu 2]], a 52,400-seat stadium in the affluent District 2 neighbourhood of Sanu-Sasso.

== History ==

=== Founding and early years (1906–1940) ===

Sanu-Sasso Prima FC was founded on 14 March 1906 by a group of Waajuri and Sikani merchants and professionals in District 2 of Sanu-Sasso, the administrative capital of Asikyira. The club's founding coincided with the early development of organised football in Asikyira, which had been introduced by Burawi colonial administrators and sailors in the late 19th century. The name ''Prima'' — meaning "first" in Volisanian, reflecting the language's status as a lingua franca among the Asikyiran commercial class — was chosen to signal the club's ambition to be the preeminent sporting institution in the capital.

The club's early identity was shaped by its location in District 2, the most affluent neighbourhood of Sanu-Sasso, home to the Signare merchant class, the professional elite, and the senior civil service. Unlike the clubs founded in the working-class neighbourhoods of Kuluba and the former Libertalian territories, Prima was from its inception associated with the capital's establishment — a reputation that would shape its rivalry with [[Sanu-Sasso Kulia FC]] and define its place in Asikyiran football culture.

Prima won its first Asikyiran Premier League title in 1922 and established itself as the dominant force in capital football through the 1920s and 1930s, winning five titles before the outbreak of the [[Great Adonian War]] interrupted competitive football.

=== Post-war and the Clàssic era (1946–1969) ===

The resumption of football after the Great Adonian War coincided with the political upheaval that would culminate in the [[Simb Revolution]] of 1969. Prima, like all Asikyiran institutions, was shaped by the political currents of the period. The club's establishment identity made it a target of Simb-era reformers, who viewed the club as a symbol of the old commercial oligarchy, and Prima's management was restructured under the Revolutionary Council's sports policy in 1971.

Despite the political turbulence, the post-war period was Prima's most successful on the pitch. The club won six league titles between 1948 and 1968, including three consecutive titles from 1959 to 1961 — the first "three-peat" in Asikyiran football history. The period also saw the emergence of the '''Derbi di Sanu-Sasso''' between Prima and [[Sanu-Sasso Kulia FC]], the club of the capital's working-class Kulia district, as the most intense fixture in the Asikyiran calendar.

=== Simb period and restructuring (1969–1996) ===

The Simb Revolution's impact on Prima was profound. The Revolutionary Council's sports policy, which sought to democratise football and break the hold of the commercial elite on the major clubs, placed Prima under the administration of the Asikyiran Sports Development Authority (ASDA) in 1971. The ASDA restructured the club's governance, expanded its youth development programme, and mandated the inclusion of players from the cooperative farm system — a policy that, despite its coercive origins, broadened Prima's talent pool and contributed to the club's on-field success in the 1970s and 1980s.

Prima won two league titles during the Simb period (1974, 1983) and established its youth academy — the '''Akademiya Njaxas''' — as the finest in Asikyira. The academy produced a generation of players who would dominate Asikyiran football in the 1990s and 2000s, including several who starred for the [[Asikyiran national football team|Asikyiran national team]] at the [[2006 AFA World Cup]].

=== Modern era and continental success (1996–present) ===

The adoption of the 1996 constitution and the restoration of multi-party democracy brought renewed investment and commercial interest to Asikyiran football. Prima, freed from the ASDA's direct control but retaining the Authority as a majority shareholder, entered the modern era as the country's wealthiest and most professionally managed club.

The club's greatest achievement came in continental competition. Prima won the [[Abyalan Champions' Cup]] in 2012, defeating [[Volisania City FC]] in the final, and repeated the triumph in 2021 with a victory over [[Castejón FC]]. The 2021 campaign, in which a 21-year-old [[Yuto Mifà]] scored nine goals in eleven matches, is regarded as the finest in the club's history and established Prima's reputation as one of the elite clubs of Adonian football.

Domestically, Prima has won three league titles since 1996 (2003, 2018, 2024), maintaining its position as the most successful club in Asikyiran history despite increased competition from [[Kuluba City FC]] and the resurgent [[Sanu-Sasso Kulia FC]].

== Crest and colours ==

Prima's traditional colours are red and white, said to represent the blood and spirit of the Asikyiran people. The club's crest features a stylised panther — the njaxas, a symbol of power and stealth in Waajuri folklore — above a shield bearing the club's initials "SSP" and the year of founding. The crest was redesigned in 1997 following the end of the Simb period, replacing the revolutionary iconography that had been imposed on the club during the ASDA administration with a design that referenced both the njaxas tradition and the club's pre-revolutionary heritage.

== Stadium ==

{{main|Stadiu di Distrettu 2}}

Prima has played its home matches at the [[Stadiu di Distrettu 2]] since the stadium's construction in 1938. The stadium, located in the heart of District 2, has a capacity of 52,400 and is the largest club stadium in Asikyira. It was extensively renovated in 2008 ahead of the [[2010 AFA World Cup]], when it hosted several group-stage matches, and again in 2019 with the addition of corporate hospitality suites and a modern training complex.

The stadium is known for its distinctive atmosphere — the District 2 crowd, drawn from the capital's professional and commercial classes, is regarded as the most knowledgeable and demanding in Asikyiran football. The south stand, known as the '''Tribuna Njaxas''', is the traditional home of the club's ultras, who maintain a fierce rivalry with the Kulia ultras across the city.

== Rivalries ==

=== Derbi di Sanu-Sasso ===

{{main|Derbi di Sanu-Sasso}}

Prima's most significant rivalry is with [[Sanu-Sasso Kulia FC]], the club of the capital's working-class Kulia district. The '''Derbi di Sanu-Sasso''' is the most intense fixture in Asikyiran football, dividing the capital along class lines: Prima's affluent District 2 support against Kulia's working-class base. The rivalry has its origins in the social geography of Sanu-Sasso and has been intensified by the political divisions of the Simb period, when Kulia was associated with the revolutionary movement and Prima with the old establishment.

=== Rivalry with Kuluba City FC ===

Prima's rivalry with [[Kuluba City FC]] — the dominant club of Asikyira's economic capital — reflects the broader competition between Sanu-Sasso and Kuluba for political and economic primacy in Asikyira. The fixture, known as the '''Derbi di Nasyoon''' (National Derby), has become increasingly significant in the post-Simb era as both clubs have invested heavily in squad building and continental competition.

